2026-11-24 19:10 Cause 1 (booleans; t/share_suites.t, t/sim/sehen.t): JSON::MaybeXS::is_bool sees a YAML true/false (core boolean from YAML::XS) and a Perl !!0 only through builtin::is_bool, i.e. perl 5.36+, and only from JSON::MaybeXS 1.004006 on. On 5.24-5.34 demo-lamp/demo-sehen fail lint ($.on: erwartet boolean). Decision (mine, per brief): raise the floor to perl 5.036 and JSON::MaybeXS 1.004006 instead of a fallback. Considered: loading YAML booleans as JSON::PP::Boolean only on old perls makes the state differ per perl (blessed refs; false renders 0 instead of empty in templates) - no longer deterministic across perls; a flag heuristic (dualvar empty/0 with public IOK/NOK) misreads a float 1.0 that was used as an integer as true. Perl < 5.36 has no boolean apart from empty/1, so the floor is the honest declaration; those perls get NA instead of FAIL. Test t/booleans.t: red against the old cpanfile, green after. Measuring on perl:5.36 in docker.

2026-11-24 19:28 Cause 2 (t/sim/sehen.t, t/dsl/loader.t, t/runner.t: demo-lamp/demo-sehen do not load; 'no warning (temperature …)'): moot with the 5.036 floor of cause 1. The load failures are the boolean lint of cause 1; the warning is Langertha's Role/HTTP.pm testing 'scalar %args > 0', which yields '5/8' on perl < 5.26 ('Argument "5/8" isn't numeric', in the 5.24 reports). No own commit. Also found: that line in Langertha (Role/HTTP.pm, around line 169) warns on perl < 5.26; Langertha's own board, not fixed here. Also found: t/dsl/loader.t runs its warning checks through IPC::Open3 with undef as the error handle, so stderr is mixed into stdout.

2026-11-24 19:29 Cause 3 (t/cli/errors.t, 'a directory as report file'): on the BSDs and Hurd read(2) on a directory returns its entries (the report read as garbage JSON), on Windows sysopen fails with 'Permission denied'. Fix in lib: Report->read refuses a directory itself with EISDIR's text (POSIX::strerror) as a Path::Tiny::Error, so every system says 'Is a directory'. Test: t/cli/errors.t replays both answers by wrapping Path::Tiny::slurp_raw; red before (tests 21, 27, the messages of the reports), green after.

2026-11-24 19:30 Cause 4 (32-bit IV, i686): on ivsize=4 a sum or product past 2**32-1 becomes a double and the bit operators clamp it to 2**32-1 (U_V). Random's _mul32/splitmix32 and Haystack's seed mix overflowed, so every draw was 4294967295 and every seed gave the same cases/text. Fix: Random::_mul32 on 16-bit limbs, new _add32, every intermediate below 2**32; Haystack's seed mix uses them. 64-bit output unchanged (pinned values in t/random.t, 'same bytes as cai-platform' in t/haystack.t). Test t/random_32bit.t with t/lib/Holmgang/UV32.pm, a number that computes as a 32-bit-IV perl does; against the old lib it reproduces the reports exactly (seed 4711 -> 4294967295, seed 0 dice 1 1 …, pick reaches 5 of 8), green after. awk (t/sim/linux_messung.t): Shell::Filter formatted computed values with sprintf '%d', which wraps past 2**31-1 on 32 bit; now '%d' only where it round-trips, else '%.0f' (64-bit output byte-identical). Test t/sim/awk_int32.t emulates 32-bit '%d' via CORE::GLOBAL::sprintf; red before with the report's '-0.5 GB', green after.

2026-11-24 19:33 Cause 5 (Windows; 5.42 and 5.24 reports): (a) Loader->list/locate split search directories at ':', so 'C:/…' fell apart (t/loader.t 'locate', t/dsl/loader.t). Fix: split at $Config{path_sep} (';' on Windows), as PATH does; POD says so. Test in t/loader.t: path_sep replaced by ';' and a root with ':' in its name; red before (locate undef), green after; the existing tests join with path_sep. (b) t/haystack.t ran its child as a multi-line -e, which a Windows command line breaks ('syntax error at -e line 1'); the program now goes into a file (test fix only). (c) The ~20 further files on the 5.24 box: JSON::MaybeXS without true/false (floor 1.004006, cause 1) and an old YAML::XS refusing '2001:db8::2' in a flow mapping ('found unexpected :', t/grader_rules.t). Measured in docker perl:5.36: YAML::XS 0.76 fails with the reports' message, 0.77 parses -> requires YAML::XS 0.77; t/yaml_flow_colon.t checks the parse and the floor, red before (floor), green after. (d) t/cli/errors.t: cause 3.

